<p>The staff evidence pack gathers what Care Core records about your staff into one page you can show an inspector or a commissioner, or use for your own review. It is under <strong>Evidence</strong> in the menu, for managers and administrators.</p>
<h2>What it shows</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Who:</strong> everyone in post on the date you choose, for one team or for all staff. Change the date to see how things stood earlier.</li>
<li><strong>Registrations</strong> (for example SSSC): the latest of each type, its number and expiry date, and whether it is in date, expires within 60 days, or has expired.</li>
<li><strong>Supervision and appraisal:</strong> the latest of each, how many supervisions were recorded in the 12 months before, and the next date recorded as due.</li>
<li><strong>Mandatory training:</strong> the latest record of each course marked mandatory, with its expiry.</li>
<li><strong>Dates that have passed:</strong> one list of everything recorded that is past its date: an expired registration, expired mandatory training, a supervision or appraisal recorded as due with nothing newer.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What it does not do</h2>
<p>It does not rate anyone or say your service is compliant. How often supervision should happen and which training is required are for your organisation and your regulator to decide, so the pack only reports what was recorded and which recorded dates have passed. Someone with “none recorded” may simply not have had it entered yet.</p>
<h2>Print or download</h2>
<p>Use your browser's print command on the page, or <strong>Download spreadsheet (CSV)</strong> for one row per person. Each time you print or download, Care Core records who did it in the activity log. The pack leaves out dates of birth, bank details, National Insurance numbers and addresses.</p>
